Z||000000||1FieroGTRacingInc||12-17-2000||07:51 PM||||The little gas canister behind the air filter(v6)..  It's leaking gas out around of the canister, I CAN'T find exactly where!! The car started missing, would'nt stay running at all!!!! it seem's like it is getting WAAAAAAY too much fuel or not dumping back enough fuel into the tank??  i dont know!! I did just through changing my fuel pump out!! IS IT POSSIBLE THAT I CONNECTED THE 2 SMALLER FUEL LINES UP BACKWARD'S?? I just thought of this???  would hooking these up backward's cause this?? I think that I need a FieroGod for this, maybe just this forum!! You people are like FieroGod's to me!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Thank's     steve||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FieroGTRacingInc||12-17-2000||09:16 PM||||Come on I guess the God's are'nt on line right now.....   lol||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-17-2000||09:34 PM||||Could be a few things, hoses may be one of them, but here's what my Helms manual says:<P>"RESULTS OF INCORRECT OPERATION:<BR>    - Poor Idle, stalling, and poor drivability can be caused by:<P>   Inoperative purge valve<BR>   Damaged Canister<BR>   Hoses split, cracked and or, not connected to the proper tubes."<P>later on it says that if there is liquid fuel leaking from around the bottom of the canister, you need to replace it.  I believe the one from the FieroStore runs about $50.<P>Hope this helps<BR>     <BR><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FieroGTRacingInc||12-17-2000||10:58 PM||||Thank's Joe...   If I replace the canister, Do you think I will need to *switch* the fuel hoses on the fuel lines at the rear of the fuel tank?    Thank's   Steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-18-2000||10:49 AM||||Heres the diagram out of my manual.  The line with no arrows in it is a vacuum line for the purge valve.  Otherwise I think this diagram should help, along with this excerpt from the haynes manual<P>"Although it is impossible to confuse the fuel filler and breather hoses (one is much larger in diameter than the other), it is possible to mix up the three smaller hoses.  To avoid confusion during reinstallation, note that the fuel feed (high pressure) line has two screw-type hose clamps, and the return line only has one.  The vent line to the charcoal vapor canister has a spring type clamp."<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Eecs.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||12-18-2000||06:12 PM||||Might sound crazy, but if your gas cap is defective, the gas tank can become either under or overpressurized, which can lead to the canister being saturated with gas.<P>Overfilling the tank can also do this. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-18-2000||08:54 PM||||yes, you may have put the lines on the fuel tank wrong. It would take a pretty good amount of liquid to flood the vapor can to where it's comming out the bottom. since this just happened after changing the fuel pump.....<P>BTW. the vapor can is now ruined. You'll need to replace it. It's mainly an emmisions device but it also saves you $ on gas that would evaporate and be wasted.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
